      "block_id": "b0001",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In Godot 4, the @rpc annotation replaced the old remote, puppet, and master\nkeywords. If your function doesn't have an @rpc annotation, calling .rpc()\non it will silently do nothing. There is no runtime error or warning — the\ncall is simply discarded. The same silent drop happens if a non-authority\npeer tries to call an \"authority\" RPC.",
      "heading_path": [
        "The @rpc Annotation"
      ],
      "level": null,
